Talent Profile – MLOps Engineer
1 x FTE | Fixed-term 6 month contract with possibility of extension | On-shore
Hiring team	Data Science & Analytics	Hiring managers	Robert Franklin + John Blundell
Role type	IT augment / fixed-term contractor	Location	On-shore; UK hybrid pattern to be confirmed
Tooling	Azure + Databricks	Start	As soon as available / onboarding complete

Role purpose
•	Provide on-shore MLOps engineering capability to operationalise completed Data Science models through the Boots model deployment framework.
•	Initially flex across MLOps, data engineering and platform tasks while the team and operating model mature.
•	End goal: take completed models from Data Scientists, run them through the deployment framework, then monitor them over time.
Core responsibilities
•	Work with Data Scientists to package completed models and prepare deployment-ready artefacts, configuration and documentation.
•	Build/adapt Databricks jobs, workflows, notebooks and pipelines for batch scoring, model outputs and, where required, serving patterns.
•	Support early data engineering needs: PySpark/Python pipelines, SQL, feature tables, model input/output tables, validation and data quality checks.
•	Implement model monitoring covering job health, failures, data/output checks, model performance indicators and alerting where available.
•	Maintain CI/CD, Git-based development and controlled environment promotion in Azure/Databricks aligned to Boots platform standards.
•	Collaborate with Data Lynx Platform Engineering, DevOps, Cloud/CCoE, RunOps and security teams on RBAC, secrets, access and operational handover.
•	Create concise runbooks for deployment, monitoring, troubleshooting, rollback considerations and support ownership.
Skills, experience and assessment
Essential	Desirable	Interview focus
Azure; Databricks; Python; PySpark; SQL; Databricks Jobs/Workflows; Delta/Lakehouse concepts; CI/CD; operational ML lifecycle; ability to bridge Data Science and production engineering.	MLflow/model registry; Unity Catalog; Databricks Model Serving; Azure DevOps pipelines; Terraform/Bicep; observability; retail/personalisation/forecasting/recommendation use cases; ITSM/runbooks.	How they productionise a notebook/model artefact; monitoring design; data engineering examples; CI/CD across environments; RBAC/secrets/security; handover into support.

Key deliverables and success measures
•	Repeatable route for receiving completed models and preparing them for deployment through the MLOps framework.
•	Deployment-ready Databricks workflows/jobs and configuration for priority models.
•	Monitoring approach for operational health, failures, data quality/output anomalies and ongoing model performance where data is available.
•	Feature/input/output tables and validation logic needed to support model execution.
•	Runbooks and support artefacts enabling transition from Data Science development to operational support.
•	Reusable improvements that reduce bespoke effort for future model deployments.
Candidate profile summary for suppliers
•	Look for an engineer who has genuinely deployed and operated ML workloads, not just built models. They must be comfortable doing some data engineering while the capability ramps up.
•	Must be on-shore and able to work closely with Data Science & Analytics, Data Lynx, platform, DevOps and security stakeholders in a governed enterprise environment.

